g the Preparer."}, {id: "M3.03-R05", module: "M3", moduleName: "Technical Execution & Audit Fieldwork", feature: "Three-Tier Review Matrix & Workflow\n                            Governance", text: "Summary Review Memorandum (SRM):", haystack: "M3.03-R05 Three-Tier Review Matrix & Workflow\n                            Governance Summary Review Memorandum (SRM):"}, {id: "M3.03-R06", module: "M3", moduleName: "Technical Execution & Audit Fieldwork", feature: "Three-Tier Review Matrix & Workflow\n                            Governance", text: "Auto-compiled upon Manager approval of all workprograms.", haystack: "M3.03-R06 Three-Tier Review Matrix & Workflow\n                            Governance Auto-compiled upon Manager approval of all workprograms."}, {id: "M3.03-R07", module: "M3", moduleName: "Technical Execution & Audit Fieldwork", feature: "Three-Tier Review Matrix & Workflow\n                            Governance", text: "Summarizes high-level audit variances, adjustments (AJEs), unadjusted differences against SAD/PM, and significant accounting estimates.", haystack: "M3.03-R07 Three-Tier Review Matrix & Workflow\n                            Governance Summarizes high-level audit variances, adjustments (AJEs), unadjusted differences against SAD/PM, and significant accounting estimates."}, {id: "M3.03-R08", module: "M3", moduleName: "Technical Execution & Audit Fieldwork", feature: "Three-Tier Review Matrix & Workflow\n                            Governance", text: "Approver Clearance: Partner conducts targeted reviews of high-risk (Red) areas and the SRM, formally signing off to unlock reporting.", haystack: "M3.03-R08 Three-Tier Review Matrix & Workflow\n                            Governance Approver Clearance: Partner conducts targeted reviews of high-risk (Red) areas and the SRM, formally signing off to unlock reporting."}, {id: "M3.04-R01", module: "M3", moduleName: "Technical Execution & Audit Fieldwork", feature: "Third-Party Confirmations Dashboard", text: "Centralized tracking grid for Bank, Accounts Receivable, Accounts Payable, Inventory, and Legal confirmations.", haystack: "M3.04-R01 Third-Party Confirmations Dashboard Centralized tracking grid for Bank, Accounts Receivable, Accounts Payable, Inventory, and Legal confirmations."}, {id: "M3.04-R02", module: "M3", moduleName: "Technical Execution & Audit Fieldwork", feature: "Third-Party Confirmations Dashboard", text: "Holding Letter Blocker: If any confirmation marked as Critical remains unreturned, the system blocks the release of the final audit report and auto-generates a \"Pending Confirmation / Holding Letter\" to client management.", haystack: "M3.04-R02 Third-Party Confirmations Dashboard Holding Letter Blocker: If any confirmation marked as Critical remains unreturned, the system blocks the release of the final audit report and auto-generates a \"Pending Confirmation / Holding Letter\" to client management."}, {id: "M4.01-R01", module: "M4", moduleName: "Reporting & Final Deliverables", feature: "Audit Opinion Selection Engine (ISA 700 /\n                            705)", text: "Dedicated dropdown selector accessible exclusively by the Engagement Partner:", haystack: "M4.01-R01 Audit Opinion Selection Engine (ISA 700 /\n                            705) Dedicated dropdown selector accessible exclusively by the Engagement Partner:"}, {id: "M4.01-R02", module: "M4", moduleName: "Reporting & Final Deliverables", feature: "Audit Opinion Selection Engine (ISA 700 /\n                            705)", text: "1. Clean / Unqualified Opinion", haystack: "M4.01-R02 Audit Opinion Selection Engine (ISA 700 /\n                            705) 1. Clean / Unqualified Opinion"}, {id: "M4.01-R03", module: "M4", moduleName: "Reporting & Final Deliverables", feature: "Audit Opinion Selection Engine (ISA 700 /\n                            705)", text: "2. Qualified Opinion", haystack: "M4.01-R03 Audit Opinion Selection Engine (ISA 700 /\n                            705) 2. Qualified Opinion"}, {id: "M4.01-R04", module: "M4", moduleName: "Reporting & Final Deliverables", feature: "Audit Opinion Selection Engine (ISA 700 /\n                            705)", text: "3. Disclaimer of Opinion", haystack: "M4.01-R04 Audit Opinion Selection Engine (ISA 700 /\n                            705) 3. Disclaimer of Opinion"}, {id: "M4.01-R05", module: "M4", moduleName: "Reporting & Final Deliverables", feature: "Audit Opinion Selection Engine (ISA 700 /\n                            705)", text: "4. Adverse Opinion", haystack: "M4.01-R05 Audit Opinion Selection Engine (ISA 700 /\n                            705) 4. Adverse Opinion"}, {id: "M4.01-R06", module: "M4", moduleName: "Reporting & Final Deliverables", feature: "Audit Opinion Selection Engine (ISA 700 /\n                            705)", text: "Conditional Qualification Builder: Selecting Qualified, Disclaimer, or Adverse dynamically prompts the Partner to select the affected FSLI and input a mandatory textual justification. The system injects this text directly into the \"Basis for Qualified/Modified Opinion\" paragraph in compliance with ISA 705.", haystack: "M4.01-R06 Audit Opinion Selection Engine (ISA 700 /\n                            705) Conditional Qualification Builder: Selecting Qualified, Disclaimer, or Adverse dynamically prompts the Partner to select the affected FSLI and input a mandatory textual justification. The system injects this text directly into the \"Basis for Qualified/Modified Opinion\" paragraph in compliance with ISA 705."}, {id: "M4.01-R07", module: "M4", moduleName: "Reporting & Final Deliverables", feature: "Audit Opinion Selection Engine (ISA 700 /\n                            705)", text: "Digital Credentials: Embeds the Partner's digital signature and official firm seal onto the final certified document.", haystack: "M4.01-R07 Audit Opinion Selection Engine (ISA 700 /\n                            705) Digital Credentials: Embeds the Partner's digital signature and official firm seal onto the final certified document."}, {id: "M4.02-R01", module: "M4", moduleName: "Reporting & Final Deliverables", feature: "Mandatory 5-Part Commercial Deliverables\n                            Bundle", text: "Once the Partner authorizes the file, the system compiles the final package:", haystack: "M4.02-R01 Mandatory 5-Part Commercial Deliverables\n                            Bundle Once the Partner authorizes the file, the system compiles the final package:"}, {id: "M4.02-R02", module: "M4", moduleName: "Reporting & Final Deliverables", feature: "Mandatory 5-Part Commercial Deliverables\n                            Bundle", text: "1. Independent Auditor's Report & Audited Financial Statements: Certified, sealed, and digitally signed PDF.", haystack: "M4.02-R02 Mandatory 5-Part Commercial Deliverables\n                            Bundle 1. Independent Auditor's Report & Audited Financial Statements: Certified, sealed, and digitally signed PDF."}, {id: "M4.02-R03", module: "M4", moduleName: "Reporting & Final Deliverables", feature: "Mandatory 5-Part Commercial Deliverables\n                            Bundle", text: "2. Management Letter: Structured internal control observations report (Deficiency → Impact → Auditor Recommendation).", haystack: "M4.02-R03 Mandatory 5-Part Commercial Deliverables\n                            Bundle 2. Management Letter: Structured internal control observations report (Deficiency → Impact → Auditor Recommendation)."}, {id: "M4.02-R04", module: "M4", moduleName: "Reporting & Final Deliverables", feature: "Mandatory 5-Part Commercial Deliverables\n                            Bundle", text: "3. Letter of Representation (LOR): Formatted representation template populated with engagement figures, ready to be exported for printing on client letterhead, signed by executive management, and re-uploaded.", haystack: "M4.02-R04 Mandatory 5-Part Commercial Deliverables\n                            Bundle 3. Letter of Representation (LOR): Formatted representation template populated with engagement figures, ready to be exported for printing on client letterhead, signed by executive management, and re-uploaded."}, {id: "M4.02-R05", module: "M4", moduleName: "Reporting & Final Deliverables", feature: "Mandatory 5-Part Commercial Deliverables\n                            Bundle", text: "4. Management Correspondences Audit Trail: Summary of all formal audit inquiries, confirmation results, and cleared queries.", haystack: "M4.02-R05 Mandatory 5-Part Commercial Deliverables\n                            Bundle 4. Management Correspondences Audit Trail: Summary of all formal audit inquiries, confirmation results, and cleared queries."}, {id: "M4.02-R06", module: "M4", moduleName: "Reporting & Final Deliverables", feature: "Mandatory 5-Part Commercial Deliverables\n                            Bundle", text: "5. Final Balance Fee Note: Automated trigger generating the invoice for the remaining 50% professional fee balance.", haystack: "M4.02-R06 Mandatory 5-Part Commercial Deliverables\n                            Bundle 5. Final Balance Fee Note: Automated trigger generating the invoice for the remaining 50% professional fee balance."}, {id: "M4.03-R01", module: "M4", moduleName: "Reporting & Final Deliverables", feature: "Regulatory File Lock (ISA 230)", text: "Enforce an automated 60-day regulatory file completion countdown timer starting from the date of the Partner's signature.", haystack: "M4.03-R01 Regulatory File Lock (ISA 230) Enforce an automated 60-day regulatory file completion countdown timer starting from the date of the Partner's signature."}, {id: "M4.03-R02", module: "M4", moduleName: "Reporting & Final Deliverables", feature: "Regulatory File Lock (ISA 230)", text: "Upon timer expiration (or manual Partner command), convert the entire engagement archive to Read-Only status. Deletions, modifications, and overwrites are permanently blocked.", haystack: "M4.03-R02 Regulatory File Lock (ISA 230) Upon timer expiration (or manual Partner command), convert the entire engagement archive to Read-Only status. Deletions, modifications, and overwrites are permanently blocked."}, {id: "M4.03-R03", module: "M4", moduleName: "Reporting & Final Deliverables", feature: "Regulatory File Lock (ISA 230)", text: "Maintain an immutable, timestamped audit log of all system actions, reviews, and sign-offs.", haystack: "M4.03-R03 Regulatory File Lock (ISA 230) Maintain an immutable, timestamped audit log of all system actions, reviews, and sign-offs."}, {id: "M5.01-R01", module: "M5", moduleName: "Practice Analytics & Internal Bookkeeping", feature: "Real-Time Profitability & Utilization\n                            Analytics", text: "Tiered Charge-Out Rates Engine:", haystack: "M5.01-R01 Real-Time Profitability & Utilization\n                            Analytics Tiered Charge-Out Rates Engine:"}, {id: "M5.01-R02", module: "M5", moduleName: "Practice Analytics & Internal Bookkeeping", feature: "Real-Time Profitability & Utilization\n                            Analytics", text: "Engagement Partner: 1,000 QAR / hour", haystack: "M5.01-R02 Real-Time Profitability & Utilization\n                            Analytics Engagement Partner: 1,000 QAR / hour"}, {id: "M5.01-R03", module: "M5", moduleName: "Practice Analytics & Internal Bookkeeping", feature: "Real-Time Profitability & Utilization\n                            Analytics", text: "Audit Manager: 750 QAR / hour", haystack: "M5.01-R03 Real-Time Profitability & Utilization\n                            Analytics Audit Manager: 750 QAR / hour"}, {id: "M5.01-R04", module: "M5", moduleName: "Practice Analytics & Internal Bookkeeping", feature: "Real-Time Profitability & Utilization\n                            Analytics", text: "Audit Supervisor / Senior: 500 QAR / hour", haystack: "M5.01-R04 Real-Time Profitability & Utilization\n                            Analytics Audit Supervisor / Senior: 500 QAR / hour"}, {id: "M5.01-R05", module: "M5", moduleName: "Practice Analytics & Internal Bookkeeping", feature: "Real-Time Profitability & Utilization\n                            Analytics", text: "Audit Associate / Junior: 200 QAR / hour", haystack: "M5.01-R05 Real-Time Profitability & Utilization\n                            Analytics Audit Associate / Junior: 200 QAR / hour"}, {id: "M5.01-R06", module: "M5", moduleName: "Practice Analytics & Internal Bookkeeping", feature: "Real-Time Profitability & Utilization\n                            Analytics", text: "Engagement Profitability Calculation:", haystack: "M5.01-R06 Real-Time Profitability & Utilization\n                            Analytics Engagement Profitability Calculation:"}, {id: "M5.01-R07", module: "M5", moduleName: "Practice Analytics & Internal Bookkeeping", feature: "Real-Time Profitability & Utilization\n                            Analytics", text: "Engagement Profitability = Contracted Audit Fee - Σ (Staff Hours Logged × Charge-Out Rate)", haystack: "M5.01-R07 Real-Time Profitability & Utilization\n                            Analytics Engagement Profitability = Contracted Audit Fee - Σ (Staff Hours Logged × Charge-Out Rate)"}, {id: "M5.01-R08", module: "M5", moduleName: "Practice Analytics & Internal Bookkeeping", feature: "Real-Time Profitability & Utilization\n                            Analytics", text: "Track budget vs. actual hours variance per engagement phase to evaluate realization rates and staff performance.", haystack: "M5.01-R08 Real-Time Profitability & Utilization\n                            Analytics Track budget vs. actual hours variance per engagement phase to evaluate realization rates and staff performance."}, {id: "M5.02-R01", module: "M5", moduleName: "Practice Analytics & Internal Bookkeeping", feature: "Practice Ledger & Internal\n                            Bookkeeping", text: "Dedicated internal operational accounting ledger to record:", haystack: "M5.02-R01 Practice Ledger & Internal\n                            Bookkeeping Dedicated internal operational accounting ledger to record:"}, {id: "M5.02-R02", module: "M5", moduleName: "Practice Analytics & Internal Bookkeeping", feature: "Practice Ledger & Internal\n                            Bookkeeping", text: "Office Rent & Facility Costs", haystack: "M5.02-R02 Practice Ledger & Internal\n                            Bookkeeping Office Rent & Facility Costs"}, {id: "M5.02-R03", module: "M5", moduleName: "Practice Analytics & Internal Bookkeeping", feature: "Practice Ledger & Internal\n                            Bookkeeping", text: "Staff Salaries & Benefits", haystack: "M5.02-R03 Practice Ledger & Internal\n                            Bookkeeping Staff Salaries & Benefits"}, {id: "M5.02-R04", module: "M5", moduleName: "Practice Analytics & Internal Bookkeeping", feature: "Practice Ledger & Internal\n                            Bookkeeping", text: "Partner Withdrawals", haystack: "M5.02-R04 Practice Ledger & Internal\n                            Bookkeeping Partner Withdrawals"}, {id: "M5.02-R05", module: "M5", moduleName: "Practice Analytics & Internal Bookkeeping", feature: "Practice Ledger & Internal\n                            Bookkeeping", text: "Petty Cash Expenses", haystack: "M5.02-R05 Practice Ledger & Internal\n                            Bookkeeping Petty Cash Expenses"}, {id: "M5.02-R06", module: "M5", moduleName: "Practice Analytics & Internal Bookkeeping", feature: "Practice Ledger & Internal\n                            Bookkeeping", text: "Internal Financial Reporting: Generate an internal firm Trial Balance, Monthly Profit & Loss Statement, and Client Accounts Receivable Aging Schedule (tracking 50% Advance and 50% Final Fee payments).", haystack: "M5.02-R06 Practice Ledger & Internal\n                            Bookkeeping Internal Financial Reporting: Generate an internal firm Trial Balance, Monthly Profit & Loss Statement, and Client Accounts Receivable Aging Schedule (tracking 50% Advance and 50% Final Fee payments)."}]
currentContent = [cuDecHead, cuDecisions, cuKeyHead, cuKeyTable, cuKeyFlow, cuKeyText, cuPhaseHead, cuPhaseTable, cuTaskFlow, cuWorkflowText]
cuDecHead = CardHeader("Approved decision overlays", "Operative overlays on the historical baseline")
cuDecisions = MarkDownRenderer("## Approved deviations\n\nThe entries below are operative decision overlays, and the source requirements that follow are preserved for provenance. The approved or accepted decision records here control current interpretation where source prose differs; a decision does not prove implementation, live-provider acceptance or qualified professional treatment. Do not rewrite an executed client contract or infer a professional decision from this specification.\n\n- **ADR-0002 (Angular canonical UI):** Angular 22 is the canonical user interface. The Blazor rollback host was retired by owner decision and merged as `e7ebe27c`; retirement does not mean migration parity or rollback acceptance was established. Affects the header architecture row.\n- **ADR-0003 (Microsoft sign-in for the client portal):** no temporary passwords are emailed or stored; the first-sign-in requirement of the Microsoft identity path applies. For newly converted clients, portal access also requires both keys, activation and the paid advance. Live tenant acceptance remains separate. Affects the §3.1 portal box and the §4.1.5 portal bullets.\n- **ADR-0004 (lifecycle as a derived projection):** the §5 stages are computed from gate records and never stored or set directly. Affects §5.\n- **ADR-0005 and ADR-0016 (visual appearance and certificate signing):** the PNG signature and seal remain the visible appearance. A firm-held X.509 certificate can sign the final report; when certificate signing is required, missing or invalid certificate material fails closed with no image-only fallback. eSignature providers and Purview remain out of scope. The firm's real-certificate and legal acceptance, and whether production must require certificate signing, remain separate gates. Affects §4.1.4 and §§4.4.1–4.4.2.\n- **ADR-0006 (one SharePoint site per client; Full Control for assigned staff):** the site and staff-access decision does not establish archive immutability or provider read-only protection. The archive-copy rule is controlled by ADR-0009 below.\n- **ADR-0007 (approved 50/50 fee milestones and draft-only automation):** the gated engagement letter creates the reviewed fee agreement and its advance and balance milestones. Optional automation is off by default and creates invoice drafts only: the advance draft is eligible after the letter; the balance draft is eligible only after the advance is paid and the linked financial package is released. A draft is not approved, posted, sent or collected. A draft-report date alone is not the balance-invoice trigger. Preserve the terms and evidence of already accepted or executed contracts. Affects §§3.1, 3.4, 4.1.2, 4.1.5 and 4.4.2.\n- **ADR-0009 (archive authority, from spike SPK-01):** the append-only release and archive store is authoritative for issued evidence. A separate read-only SharePoint archive library is a secondary copy. Its state is `OBSERVED` only after both exact file hashes and expected grants are read back; until then it remains `BLOCKED_EXTERNAL`. A local freeze does not protect the SharePoint copy, and the UI or regulator export must not claim provider immutability. Affects §4.4.3.\n- **ADR-0010 (end-of-service accrual, from STE-NXT-009):** end-of-service benefits are accrued as a provision entered by a person, not expensed only when paid. Affects §3.5.\n- **ADR-0011 and ADR-0017 (materiality without normalization):** the PBT benchmark is mapped balances excluding tax; no normalization adjustments are applied. Affects §4.2.4.\n- **ADR-0012 (unconditional advance activation gate; ACCEPTED):** activation into `PORTAL_ACTIVE_PLANNING` requires a linked fee agreement and its 50% `ADVANCE` milestone in `PAID` state, representing full payment and allocation. No configuration bypass is permitted. An invoice, partial payment or missing agreement is insufficient. This does not retroactively change an executed contract. Affects §§4.1.5 and 5.1.\n- **ADR-0017 (STE v2.2 delegated product decisions):** WhatsApp is a lead-channel label only; nothing is ingested from or sent through it, and proposals are dispatched by email. Acceptance records `EMAIL`, `SIGNED_LETTER`, `IN_PERSON` or `PHONE` (required for acceptance, optional for decline); the value labels evidence and sends nothing. Add continuance questions RV-031 (legal notice, claim or demand received; adverse when yes) and RV-032 (prior-year professional fees settled; adverse when no), preserving existing questions and historical answers. The firm week is Sunday–Thursday with Friday/Saturday as weekend and Sunday–Saturday allocation weeks; public holidays are recorded as unavailability, with no inferred holiday table, and statutory-relative milestone dates remain the rule (the dates in the source are examples). The staffed Engagement Partner is required for SRM clearance, opinion, report signing, signed-representation verification and bundle assembly. Planning approval covers current materiality and risk routing; a recorded critical-estimate flag bands Red; high inherent risk is likelihood 3 with magnitude at least 2; Amber work is performed by Senior Auditor or above and reviewed by an Audit Manager. Sampling versus full-population testing is documented senior judgment; no sample is universally required. Affects §§3.1–3.5, 4.1–4.3, 5.1–5.2 and 6.3.\n- **ADR-0018 (practice reporting bases):** approved non-billable/no-charge time counts in actual hours and cost but has no charge-out value; standard value, realization and contract contribution use approved billable time only, and missing rate/currency makes those figures unavailable. Utilization is approved billable minutes divided by capacity net of recorded unavailability; show all approved hours separately. Age every posted firm invoice (advance, final, time or other); do not include client-bookkeeping invoices, and refuse a report for an invoice bound to multiple milestones. Monthly P&L uses one row per accounting month and the same month one year earlier as comparator. The dashboard names currently staffed users at the level owning each step but grants no permissions. Apply Senior/Supervisor/Junior/Associate rate aliases wherever rates are looked up. Staff-level performance measures and visibility, facility/benefit expense taxonomy, broader fee/partial-payment policy and the professional/legal items listed in ADR-0018 remain undecided. Affects §§3.5 and 4.5.1–4.5.2.\n", "sunk")
cuKeyHead = CardHeader("Enhanced dual-key acceptance", "Both keys must be present before an Engagement Letter")
cuKeyTable = Table([Col("Key 1: client commercial acceptance", ["Missing", "Approved", "Missing or stale", "Current and valid", "Current and valid"]), Col("Key 2: Partner risk clearance", ["Missing", "Missing or stale", "Approved", "Current and unconditional", "Current and unconditional; 50% advance allocated"]), Col("Engagement Letter", ["Blocked", "Blocked", "Blocked", "Eligible for separately authorized issuance", "Eligible for separately authorized issuance"]), Col("Planning activation", ["Blocked", "Blocked", "Blocked", "Blocked until 50% advance is fully paid and allocated", "Eligible, subject to other holds and authorization checks"])])
cuKeyFlow = CodeBlock("mermaid", "sequenceDiagram\n    participant Client\n    participant CRM as Commercial Workspace\n    participant Partner\n    participant Risk as Acceptance Records\n    participant Docs as Engagement Documents\n    participant Finance\n    participant Planning\n    Client->>CRM: Accept exact dispatched quotation revision\n    CRM->>Risk: Persist commercial response evidence\n    Partner->>Risk: Review AML, KYC, independence and continuance\n    Partner->>Risk: Record current risk decision\n    CRM->>Risk: Recheck both independent approval keys\n    alt Both keys current and approved\n        Risk-->>Docs: Engagement Letter generation eligible\n        Docs->>Finance: Initiate 50 percent advance fee workflow\n        Finance->>Finance: Record and allocate payment\n        alt Advance fully paid and no outstanding hold\n            Finance-->>Planning: Activation may proceed through authorized command\n        else Unpaid, partial, stale or held\n            Finance-->>Planning: Activation blocked with exact reasons\n        end\n    else Missing or invalid approval\n        Risk-->>CRM: Block document — show missing or stale key\n    end")
cuKeyText = MarkDownRenderer("### 4.1.3 Dual-Key Onboarding Gatekeeper\n\nThe system shall strictly disallow the generation of an Engagement Letter until two independent authorization keys are marked active in the database:\n* **Key 1 (Commercial Approval):** Recorded confirmation of client quote acceptance.\n* **Key 2 (Risk Clearance):** Partner completion and digital sign-off of the Client Acceptance/Continuance Checklist (ISA 220).\n\n#### Enhanced Dual-Key Acceptance — mandatory workflow requirements for version 2.2\n\n**Approval decision matrix**\n\n| Key 1: client commercial acceptance | Key 2: Partner risk clearance | Engagement Letter | Planning activation |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Missing | Missing | Blocked | Blocked |\n| Approved | Missing or stale | Blocked | Blocked |\n| Missing or stale | Approved | Blocked | Blocked |\n| Current and valid | Current and unconditional | Eligible for separately authorized issuance | Blocked until 50% advance is fully paid and allocated |\n| Current and valid | Current and unconditional; 50% advance allocated | Eligible for separately authorized issuance | Eligible, subject to other holds and authorization checks |\n\n**Actor sequence**\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant Client\n    participant CRM as Commercial Workspace\n    participant Partner\n    participant Risk as Acceptance Records\n    participant Docs as Engagement Documents\n    participant Finance\n    participant Planning\n    Client->>CRM: Accept exact dispatched quotation revision\n    CRM->>Risk: Persist commercial response evidence\n    Partner->>Risk: Review AML, KYC, independence and continuance\n    Partner->>Risk: Record current risk decision\n    CRM->>Risk: Recheck both independent approval keys\n    alt Both keys current and approved\n        Risk-->>Docs: Engagement Letter generation eligible\n        Docs->>Finance: Initiate 50 percent advance fee workflow\n        Finance->>Finance: Record and allocate payment\n        alt Advance fully paid and no outstanding hold\n            Finance-->>Planning: Activation may proceed through authorized command\n        else Unpaid, partial, stale or held\n            Finance-->>Planning: Activation blocked with exact reasons\n        end\n    else Missing or invalid approval\n        Risk-->>CRM: Block document — show missing or stale key\n    end\n```\n\n- **Key 1 — Client Commercial Acceptance:** Capture the client's acceptance of the exact dispatched quotation revision, scope, legal entity, service route, period, currency, fee and 50/50 payment terms. Record authorized contact, response channel, timestamp and linked acceptance evidence. A changed offer requires a renewed acceptance.\n- **Key 2 — Partner Risk Clearance:** Independently require the Engagement Partner's current, unconditional client acceptance/continuance decision against the current due-diligence generation. Require AML/KYC, beneficial ownership, independence, conflicts, management integrity and other relevant risk checks. Conditional, rejected, superseded or stale decisions never clear this key.\n- **Gate outcomes:** neither key ⇒ blocked, two approvals needed; only Key 1 ⇒ awaiting Partner risk clearance; only Key 2 ⇒ awaiting client commercial acceptance; both current keys ⇒ eligible for Engagement Letter, NOT automatically activated.\n- The full 50% advance payment is a separate gate after the two keys: generate the Engagement Letter and advance invoice under their existing authorization rules; activate engagement and portal-enabled planning only after the linked 50% advance is fully paid and allocated. A partially paid or merely invoiced advance is not sufficient.\n- **Changes and exceptions:** a declined proposal returns to revision/re-dispatch or closure; a conditional or refused Partner decision returns to risk remediation and fresh unconditional review; open holds, stale commercial revisions and mismatched client/service scopes block protected operations. Never let task completion, workflow rules or staff overrides bypass these guards.\n- **Onboarding interface:** provide two independent approval cards, each showing Pending, Awaiting Evidence, Approved, Rejected or Stale as applicable, owner, time, evidence link, revision and authorized next action. Show a separate Engagement Letter readiness row and a third 50% Advance Payment card. Hide sensitive AML/KYC findings from the client portal.\n- **Audit history:** preserve the authentic approving actor, decision generation, source evidence, timestamps and reason for rejection; re-evaluate both keys at document generation and activation, and reject stale or concurrently changed inputs.\n- **Worked example:** on an accepted QAR 20,000 quotation, Partner acceptance is still mandatory before an Engagement Letter may be issued. Both keys permit letter issuance and the QAR 10,000 advance invoice, but activation waits until the full QAR 10,000 is received and allocated.\n\n*Implementation note:* the unconditional 50% advance activation gate is recorded in ADR-0012. The matrix describes required behaviour; it does not by itself prove it. Verification status is in the v2.2 delta of the gap-verification tracker.\n", "sunk")
cuPhaseHead = CardHeader("Seven-phase workflow, tasks and non-regression", "Seven display phases projected from eleven canonical states")
cuPhaseTable = Table([Col("Display phase", ["1. Client Onboarding", "2. Audit Planning", "3. Audit Fieldwork", "4. Manager Review", "5. Partner Sign-off", "6. Report and Delivery", "7. Archive and Close"]), Col("Canonical states represented", ["LEAD_INGESTION , PROPOSAL_GENERATION , DUAL_KEY_PENDING , ADVANCE_BILLING", "PORTAL_ACTIVE_PLANNING", "FIELDWORK_EXECUTION", "MANAGERIAL_REVIEW", "PARTNER_APPROVAL", "DELIVERABLE_RELEASE", "COMPLIANCE_COUNTDOWN , ARCHIVED_READ_ONLY"])])
cuTaskFlow = CodeBlock("mermaid", "flowchart LR\n    T[\"Versioned task template\"] --> RUN[\"Engagement task instances\"]\n    RUN --> AUTO[\"Task automator\"]\n    AUTO --> GOOD[\"Permitted: assignments, follow-ups, reminders and escalation\"]\n    AUTO --> G{\"Needs protected professional or financial decision?\"}\n    G -->|\"Yes\"| C[\"Submit to authorized domain command and independent actor\"]\n    G -->|\"No\"| GOOD\n    C --> V[\"Check role, client scope, evidence and current revision\"]\n    V --> E[\"Persist authentic decision and audit event\"]\n    E --> PROJ[\"Recompute canonical lifecycle projection\"]\n    classDef decision fill:#fff1d6,stroke:#b88b2c,color:#5d4316\n    class G decision")
cuWorkflowText = MarkDownRenderer("## 5.3 Display Phases and Canonical States\n\nThe eleven canonical states in §5.1 remain authoritative. Sections 6 and 7 present a simpler seven-phase user-facing workflow but do not replace these gate conditions. The diagram in §5.2 is not itself a permission model: transitions follow their underlying business commands and evidentiary gates.\n\n| Display phase | Canonical states represented |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1. Client Onboarding | `LEAD_INGESTION`, `PROPOSAL_GENERATION`, `DUAL_KEY_PENDING`, `ADVANCE_BILLING` |\n| 2. Audit Planning | `PORTAL_ACTIVE_PLANNING` |\n| 3. Audit Fieldwork | `FIELDWORK_EXECUTION` |\n| 4. Manager Review | `MANAGERIAL_REVIEW` |\n| 5. Partner Sign-off | `PARTNER_APPROVAL` |\n| 6. Report and Delivery | `DELIVERABLE_RELEASE` |\n| 7. Archive and Close | `COMPLIANCE_COUNTDOWN`, `ARCHIVED_READ_ONLY` |\n\n---\n\n# 6. Simplified Seven-Phase Engagement Workflow — New Requirements\n\n## 6.1 Purpose and mapping\n\nThis user-interface and task orchestration layer SHALL NOT modify the canonical Section 5 lifecycle state names, stage gates, reviews, or compliance evidence. Map stages as follows:\n\n- Phase 1 Client Onboarding: `LEAD_INGESTION`, `PROPOSAL_GENERATION`, `DUAL_KEY_PENDING`, `ADVANCE_BILLING`.\n- Phase 2 Audit Planning: `PORTAL_ACTIVE_PLANNING`.\n- Phase 3 Audit Fieldwork: `FIELDWORK_EXECUTION`.\n- Phase 4 Manager Review: `MANAGERIAL_REVIEW`, with procedure-level rework loop back to affected fieldwork.\n- Phase 5 Partner Sign-off: `PARTNER_APPROVAL`.\n- Phase 6 Report & Delivery: `DELIVERABLE_RELEASE`.\n- Phase 7 Archive & Close: `COMPLIANCE_COUNTDOWN` and `ARCHIVED_READ_ONLY`.\n\n## 6.2 Engagement dashboard\n\nShow a seven-step visual tracker with simple titles, responsible user, relevant milestone/date, task completion, gate readiness, explicit blockers and the next permitted action. Offer expandable phase checklists and contextual links to client, planning, financial statement line item, PBC, review, completion, finance and records workbenches. Distinguish task completion from regulatory clearance. Make the design responsive and keyboard accessible.\n\n## 6.3 Phase detail requirements\n\n- **Client Onboarding:** quotation and client response, separated dual-key approvals, Engagement Letter, 50% invoice/payment and activation eligibility.\n- **Audit Planning:** staff and deadlines, workspace provisioning, TB import, approved mapping, materiality PM/TE/SAD, risk routing and Partner planning approval. Updated inputs must invalidate stale approvals.\n- **Audit Fieldwork:** FSLI action links, workprograms, evidence, analytical reviews, sampling, preparer assignments and versioned result submission.\n- **Manager Review:** independent reviewer authority and risk-based hierarchy; mandatory comments on rejection; preserve history and route affected work back to its preparer; resolve all relevant review notes; compile a current SRM.\n- **Partner Sign-off:** review high-risk areas/SRM, select an ISA opinion and rationale when modified, and sign the final report under approved credentials.\n- **Report & Delivery:** independently evaluated critical confirmations, controlled audited statement and report delivery, management letter, LOR, correspondence, final fee note and release checkpoints.\n- **Archive & Close:** signature-anchored 60-day countdown, authorized early lock and effective local read-only freeze. Show external provider retention/protection independently; an expired timer alone is not archive success.\n\n## 6.4 Reusable practice templates\n\nPermit administrator-approved versioned templates by engagement type and industry, with editable task groups, owners, due-date offsets, dependencies, effort estimates, client requests and ad-hoc tasks. Pin a template revision to each engagement; changes to templates do not silently rewrite existing work. These templates cannot remove mandatory domain gates. Provide My Tasks, Team Work, Waiting for Client, Under Review, Rework, Overdue and Completed list filters plus Kanban/calendar views.\n\n## 6.5 Recurring audit engagements\n\nSupport creating the next annual engagement with reusable templates, prior-year client details and historical mapping suggestions. Require fresh commercial consent, current Partner continuance risk approval, current TB/materiality, professional audit review and reporting decisions. Never carry prior-year acceptance or opinion sign-offs forward as valid authorization.\n\n## 6.6 Safe workflow automation\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    T[\"Versioned task template\"] --> RUN[\"Engagement task instances\"]\n    RUN --> AUTO[\"Task automator\"]\n    AUTO --> GOOD[\"Permitted: assignments, follow-ups, reminders and escalation\"]\n    AUTO --> G{\"Needs protected professional or financial decision?\"}\n    G -->|\"Yes\"| C[\"Submit to authorized domain command and independent actor\"]\n    G -->|\"No\"| GOOD\n    C --> V[\"Check role, client scope, evidence and current revision\"]\n    V --> E[\"Persist authentic decision and audit event\"]\n    E --> PROJ[\"Recompute canonical lifecycle projection\"]\n    classDef decision fill:#fff1d6,stroke:#b88b2c,color:#5d4316\n    class G decision\n```\n\nAutomators MAY assign tasks, create follow-up checklists, set reminders and due dates, escalate overdue PBC requests and notify permitted users after genuine domain events. They SHALL NOT synthesize approvals, record payment, clear risk, approve materiality, sign an opinion, post invoices, issue release or freeze files. Every automation must reauthorize, use idempotency keys, pin current versions, log its changes and fail safely on stale inputs. Task graphs must reject dependency cycles.\n\n## 6.7 User role, security and progress rules\n\nPreparer sees assigned fieldwork/rework; Reviewer sees submissions and review notes; Partner sees acceptance, high-risk areas, opinion and release; Client sees only authorized commercial and PBC status. Calculate phase readiness from server-side records, not mutable task flags. Track task percentage separately from mandatory gate satisfaction, avoid leaking AML/KYC evidence to client users and show readable blocker reasons.\n\n## 6.8 Acceptance criteria\n\nAcceptance criteria to verify:\n\n1. All 11 canonical states map to exactly one of seven phases.\n2. Absent/one-key approvals block Engagement Letter issuance.\n3. Both keys allow the letter but do not bypass the full 50% advance.\n4. Changed offer or risk basis invalidates the affected approval.\n5. Rejection/conditional clearance and open holds cannot be overwritten through tasks.\n6. Independent reviewer and mandatory rework comments remain enforced.\n7. Open review notes and stale materiality block subsequent professional decisions.\n8. Critical confirmation cases block report release.\n9. Frozen archival state requires an effective committed lock and does not imply external immutability.\n10. Recurring templates never copy professional sign-offs as current.\n11. Scoped actors cannot access unrelated clients.\n12. Automation retries cannot duplicate or forge domain events.\n\n---\n\n# 7. Architectural Non-Regression Requirements — New\n\nAll domain commands and evidence records remain the sole authority for progression. The existing 11-stage derived lifecycle and five function modules remain unchanged. The seven-phase user experience is a deterministic presentation mapping. Task templates, personal work queues, recurring-engagement creation, deadline automation and dashboard analytics are separate supporting capabilities. All permissions, professional judgments, signed document integrity, 50/50 commercial terms and archive protections must continue to be enforced by authoritative services. Review external Microsoft identity/SharePoint/records protections separately before labelling them production compliant.\n", "sunk")
controlsContent = [ctHead, ctTable, psHead, ps0, ps1, ps2, ps3]
ctHead = CardHeader("Controls and decision ownership", "Historical controls with their source enforcement labels")
ctTable = Table([Col("ID", ["C-01", "C-02", "C-03", "C-04", "C-05", "C-06", "C-07", "C-08", "C-09", "C-10", "C-11", "C-12", "C-13"]), Col("Area", ["Onboarding", "Advance payment", "Governance", "Planning", "Fieldwork", "Reviewer", "Confirmations", "Partner", "Modified opinion", "Deliverables", "Client portal", "Archive", "Practice"]), Col("Required rule", ["Both independent keys active before Engagement Letter is generated", "50% paid and recorded before portal-active planning transition", "Partner acceptance before planning; Partner sign-off on materiality before fieldwork", "Materiality benchmark rules and ±5% manager rounding limitation", "Preparers submit all assigned FSLI tests before managerial review", "Mandatory rejection comments and Under Rework reassignment; zero open notes to advance", "Critical confirmations unreturned → report release blocked and Holding Letter generated", "Partner checks Red areas and SRM and signs final report", "Qualified / Disclaimer / Adverse require affected FSLI and rationale", "All five named deliverables + final 50% fee note", "Rejected upload requires reason; uploaded privileges freeze on final report release", "60-day countdown from Partner signature or manual lock → immutable read-only file", "Rates, time × rate, profitability and period cost reporting denominated in QAR"]), Col("Source", ["§4.1 · §5", "§3.1 · §5", "§4.2 · §5", "§4.2", "§4.3 · §5", "§4.3 · §5", "§4.3 · §5", "§4.3–4.4 · §5", "§4.4", "§4.4", "§4.1 · §4.4", "§4.4 · §5", "§4.5"]), Col("Source enforcement label", ["Hard block", "Hard block", "Hard block", "Calculation validation", "Transition gate", "Rework / gate", "Release blocker", "Exclusive approval", "Mandatory fields", "Release checklist", "Portal controls", "Irreversible control", "Financial calculation"])])
psHead = CardHeader("Original user personas", "Responsibilities as written in the source")
ps0 = MarkDownRenderer("**PREPARER — Audit Associate / Junior Auditor**\n\n- Executes assigned financial statement line item (FSLI) audit test procedures.\n- Uploads digital working papers and inputs physical binder index codes (X-1, Box 3).\n- Submits completed testing packages for managerial review.\n- Logs daily operational hours against assigned engagement tasks.", "card")
ps1 = MarkDownRenderer("**REVIEWER — Audit Senior / Audit Manager**\n\n- Verifies substantive testing and recalculated schedules.\n- Issues inline review notes and initiates the rework loop for incomplete tests.\n- Determines sampling parameters and calculates engagement materiality.\n- Prepares the Summary Review Memorandum (SRM) for the partner.\n- Tracks engagement budgets, team hours, and delivery milestones.", "card")
ps2 = MarkDownRenderer("**APPROVER — Engagement Partner**\n\n- Evaluates and signs off on the Dual-Key Acceptance Gate (AML/KYC).\n- Authorizes commercial proposals and executes Engagement Letters.\n- Clears high-risk (Red) audit areas and formally signs off on the SRM.\n- Selects the final Audit Opinion, applies digital signatures and firm seals.\n- Authorizes final deliverable bundles and enforces regulatory file locks.", "card")
ps3 = MarkDownRenderer("**CLIENT — Client Coordinator / CFO / MD**\n\n- Accesses an isolated, tokenized external workspace (PBC Portal).\n- Views requested audit documentation with real-time review status badges.\n- Uploads requested financial schedules, trial balances, and voucher evidence.\n- Receives invoices, receipts, holding letters, and final deliverables.\n- Access freezes automatically upon engagement sign-off.", "card")
lifecycleContent = [lcHead, lcSteps, lcTable]
lcHead = CardHeader("Eleven-state source register", "Derived lifecycle projection; no manually mutable stage column")
lcSteps = Steps([lcStep00, lcStep01, lcStep02, lcStep03, lcStep04, lcStep05, lcStep06, lcStep07, lcStep08, lcStep09, lcStep10])
lcStep00 = StepsItem("01 · LEAD_INGESTION", "Log inquiry, capture company and contact data. Advance when: Minimum entity and primary contact data validated → PROPOSAL_GENERATION")
lcStep01 = StepsItem("02 · PROPOSAL_GENERATION", "Build Brief Quote or Comprehensive Proposal, dispatch to client. Advance when: Proposal dispatched via Email → DUAL_KEY_PENDING")
lcStep02 = StepsItem("03 · DUAL_KEY_PENDING", "Complete Client Acceptance Checklist (AML/KYC), record client commercial approval. Advance when: Dual-Key Clearance: Both Client Acceptance AND Partner AML Approval confirmed → ADVANCE_BILLING")
lcStep03 = StepsItem("04 · ADVANCE_BILLING", "Generate Engagement Letter & 50% Advance Invoice. Advance when: 50% advance payment confirmed and recorded → PORTAL_ACTIVE_PLANNING")
lcStep04 = StepsItem("05 · PORTAL_ACTIVE_PLANNING", "Provision Client Portal, schedule team, ingest Trial Balance, calculate materiality. Advance when: Planning signed off by Partner, TB mapped to FSLIs → FIELDWORK_EXECUTION")
lcStep05 = StepsItem("06 · FIELDWORK_EXECUTION", "Execute workprograms, attach digital/physical evidence, log confirmation requests. Advance when: All assigned FSLI procedures submitted by Preparers → MANAGERIAL_REVIEW")
lcStep06 = StepsItem("07 · MANAGERIAL_REVIEW", "Review workpapers, issue review notes/rework, compile SRM. Advance when: Zero open review notes, SRM compiled, critical confirmations returned → PARTNER_APPROVAL")
lcStep07 = StepsItem("08 · PARTNER_APPROVAL", "Partner inspects SRM, reviews Red-risk areas, selects Audit Opinion. Advance when: Partner applies digital signature and firm seal → DELIVERABLE_RELEASE")
lcStep08 = StepsItem("09 · DELIVERABLE_RELEASE", "Generate 5-part deliverables package, issue 50% balance invoice, freeze client portal uploads. Advance when: Final package generated and delivered to client → COMPLIANCE_COUNTDOWN")
lcStep09 = StepsItem("10 · COMPLIANCE_COUNTDOWN", "Review final archive; Partner may trigger early lock. Advance when: 60 calendar days elapsed since signature date OR manual lock triggered → ARCHIVED_READ_ONLY")
lcStep10 = StepsItem("11 · ARCHIVED_READ_ONLY", "Read-only viewing and regulator inspection export. Advance when: File is permanently locked; modifications strictly disallowed → Terminal State")
lcTable = Table([Col("Canonical label", ["LEAD_INGESTION", "PROPOSAL_GENERATION", "DUAL_KEY_PENDING", "ADVANCE_BILLING", "PORTAL_ACTIVE_PLANNING", "FIELDWORK_EXECUTION", "MANAGERIAL_REVIEW", "PARTNER_APPROVAL", "DELIVERABLE_RELEASE", "COMPLIANCE_COUNTDOWN", "ARCHIVED_READ_ONLY"]), Col("Allowed actions — source", ["Log inquiry, capture company and contact data", "Build Brief Quote or Comprehensive Proposal, dispatch to client", "Complete Client Acceptance Checklist (AML/KYC), record client commercial approval", "Generate Engagement Letter & 50% Advance Invoice", "Provision Client Portal, schedule team, ingest Trial Balance, calculate materiality", "Execute workprograms, attach digital/physical evidence, log confirmation requests", "Review workpapers, issue review notes/rework, compile SRM", "Partner inspects SRM, reviews Red-risk areas, selects Audit Opinion", "Generate 5-part deliverables package, issue 50% balance invoice, freeze client portal uploads", "Review final archive; Partner may trigger early lock", "Read-only viewing and regulator inspection export"]), Col("Condition to advance — source", ["Minimum entity and primary contact data validated", "Proposal dispatched via Email", "Dual-Key Clearance: Both Client Acceptance AND Partner AML Approval confirmed", "50% advance payment confirmed and recorded", "Planning signed off by Partner, TB mapped to FSLIs", "All assigned FSLI procedures submitted by Preparers", "Zero open review notes, SRM compiled, critical confirmations returned", "Partner applies digital signature and firm seal", "Final package generated and delivered to client", "60 calendar days elapsed since signature date OR manual lock triggered", "File is permanently locked; modifications strictly disallowed"]), Col("Next state — source", ["PROPOSAL_GENERATION", "DUAL_KEY_PENDING", "ADVANCE_BILLING", "PORTAL_ACTIVE_PLANNING", "FIELDWORK_EXECUTION", "MANAGERIAL_REVIEW", "PARTNER_APPROVAL", "DELIVERABLE_RELEASE", "COMPLIANCE_COUNTDOWN", "ARCHIVED_READ_ONLY", "Terminal State"])])
extensionsContent = [exNote, exTable, exSrcHead, exSrcTable]
exNote = Callout("warning", "Supplied extensions are unverified", "Entries are shown as supplied; their enforcement references were not confirmed against the repository.")
exTable = Table([Col("ID", ["EXT-ACC-01", "EXT-ACC-02", "EXT-ACC-03", "EXT-ACC-04", "EXT-ACC-05", "EXT-ACC-06", "EXT-CON-01", "EXT-CON-02", "EXT-CON-03", "EXT-CON-04", "EXT-CON-05", "EXT-M365-01", "EXT-M365-02", "EXT-M365-03", "EXT-M365-04", "EXT-SEC-01", "EXT-SEC-02", "EXT-SEC-03", "EXT-SEC-04", "EXT-FIN-01", "EXT-FIN-02", "EXT-FIN-03", "EXT-FIN-04"]), Col("Area", ["Client Accounting Workspace R2R Accounting Workspace", "Client Accounting Workspace R2R Accounting Workspace", "Client Accounting Workspace R2R Accounting Workspace", "Client Accounting Workspace R2R Accounting Workspace", "Client Accounting Workspace R2R Accounting Workspace", "Client Accounting Workspace R2R Accounting Workspace", "Group Consolidation R2R Group Consolidation", "Group Consolidation R2R Group Consolidation", "Group Consolidation R2R Group Consolidation", "Group Consolidation R2R Group Consolidation", "Group Consolidation R2R Group Consolidation", "Microsoft 365 & Security Platform Security & Identity", "Microsoft 365 & Security Platform Security & Identity", "Microsoft 365 & Security Platform Security & Identity", "Microsoft 365 & Security Platform Security & Identity", "Document Release & Security Platform Security & Archiving", "Document Release & Security Platform Security & Archiving", "Document Release & Security Platform Security & Archiving", "Document Release & Security Platform Security & Archiving", "Practice Management & Finance Module 5 Practice Analytics", "Practice Management & Finance Module 5 Practice Analytics", "Practice Management & Finance Platform Core Numeric", "Practice Management & Finance Module 5 Practice Analytics"]), Col("Requirement", ["Client Accounting Profile & Reporting Context Activation: Define client entity, functional currency (QAR default), fiscal calendar, chart version, and reporting context revisions. ClientAccountingProfileService.ActivateContextAsync pins exact profile, period, and chart revisions", "Trial Balance & General Ledger Intake: Ingest client TB/GL records with service-date lineage, control totals debit=credit check, and quarantine staging for unmapped accounts. TrialBalanceIntakeService.ImportTrialBalanceAsync enforces sum(Debits) == sum(Credits) at scale(19,6)", "Chart of Accounts Versioning & FSLI Taxonomy Mappings: Versioned COA with parent-child hierarchy, normalized account codes, and deterministic mapping to standard FSLI reporting lines. ChartOfAccountsMappingService.PublishChartMappingAsync prevents cycles and unmapped posting accounts", "Adjusting Journal Entries (AJE) Maker-Checker Review: Record audit, client, and reclassification adjustments with balanced debits/credits, documented audit justification, and Partner approval. AdjustingJournalService.PostAdjustmentAsync enforces maker-checker separation and zero net balance", "Subledger Reconciliations & Lead Schedules: Automated reconciliation between general ledger accounts and subledgers (Bank, AR, AP, Fixed Assets, Inventory) with variance tracking. ReconciliationExecutionService.ReconcileSubledgerAsync matches GL balance against subledger schedule", "Typed Multi-Format Financial Statement Generation: Compile compliant Balance Sheet, Income Statement, Cash Flows (indirect), Changes in Equity, and Notes into genuine PDF, Excel, and Word packages. FinancialStatementCompilationEngine.GeneratePackageAsync builds multi-format signed packages", "ClientGroup Aggregate & Approved Consolidation Perimeter: Establish corporate group container, assign legal entity membership, and record approved consolidation perimeter boundaries. ConsolidationPerimeterService.DefinePerimeterAsync validates legal entity inclusion and parent-subsidiary roles", "Versioned Consolidation Scope & Entity Ownership Tracking: Maintain effective ownership percentages, voting rights, acquisition dates, goodwill, and Non-Controlling Interest (NCI) parameters. ConsolidationScopeService.SetOwnershipStructureAsync validates sum(ownership) and acquisition dates", "External Component Reporting Pack Intake & Multi-Currency Translation: Ingest external entity trial balances and translate foreign currency components using closing and average exchange rates. CurrencyTranslationService.TranslateComponentAsync applies closing rate to BS and average rate to P&L", "Intercompany Balance & Transaction Matching Engine: Match intercompany receivables, payables, revenues, expenses, and loans across group entities with discrepancy threshold highlighting. IntercompanyMatchingService.MatchTransactionsAsync identifies matching pairs and flags variances > threshold", "Automated Elimination Journals & Strict Component Non-Mutation: Execute consolidation eliminations (equity, intercompany, unrealized profit); NEVER post to or modify component client ledgers. ConsolidationEngine.ExecuteRunAsync creates group-only journal entries; zero writes to client DB tables", "Microsoft Entra ID OIDC Delegated Authentication: Authenticate staff and external clients via Microsoft identity platform with secure HttpOnly cookies, CSRF protection, and same-origin API. AuthenticationMiddleware validates OIDC ID token, binds immutable tid+oid, sets HttpOnly secure session cookie", "Capability-Isolated App Identities: Each Graph capability holds exactly one application role (User.Read.All, Sites.Selected, Mail.Send, User.Create, User.Invite.All, GroupMember.ReadWrite.All). GraphCapabilityTokenSource refuses token if application possesses broader or multiple Graph permissions", "Tenant Onboarding & Admin Consent with SHA-256 Nonce Verification: Admin consent flows store only SHA-256 hashes of state and nonce; optional capabilities disabled by default. M365ConsentService validates callback hash against persisted SHA-256 state; refuses unconsented tenant calls", "Dedicated Client SharePoint Sites with Scoped Sites.Selected Grants: Provision one dedicated SharePoint site per client; document worker granted write permission only to that specific site. SharePointProvisioningService requests per-site grant; rejects tenant-wide Sites.ReadWrite.All", "Authoritative Release & Immutable Archive Store: Platform release store holds primary authoritative evidence with immutable SHA-256 hash validation; immune to external tenant alterations. AuthoritativeArchiveStore.PersistIssuedEvidenceAsync computes and verifies SHA-256 hash before sealing", "Secondary SharePoint Synchronization: Synchronize read-only working copy of issued audit deliverables to client SharePoint site; platform store remains authoritative if sync fails. DurableSharePointSyncWorker replicates deliverable package; logs external failure without failing release", "Firm-Held X.509 Certificate-Based PDF Signing: Sign final audit deliverables with firm-held X.509 digital certificate and visual Partner signature/seal; cloud eSignature providers excluded. PdfDigitalSigningService signs deliverable using firm private key; verifies certificate validity and revocation", "60-Day Mandatory Regulatory Archive Lock: Strict 60-day countdown from Partner signature or manual Partner lock seals all working papers, schedules, and evidence into immutable read-only state. ArchiveLockWorker automatically triggers lockdown at Day 60; database fences prevent subsequent edits", "Practice Time Attribution with Approved FSLI Mapping Lineage: Engagement tasks and staff timesheet entries must pin the exact approved FSLI mapping and audit destination. TimesheetService.RecordTimeAsync validates that FsliId references an active approved FSLI in engagement scope", "Sunday-Thursday Working Week & Non-Billable Charge-Out Rate: Official firm working week is Sunday through Thursday; non-billable time carries 0 charge-out rate for firm realization calculations. PracticeCalendarService enforces standard Sunday-Thursday work week; non-billable hours carry rate = 0.00", "Six-Decimal Monetary Scale & Banker's Rounding: Financial amounts stored as numeric(19,6); midpoint rounding follows MidpointRounding.ToEven default; explicit scale conversion to display currency. FinancialMoneyValueObject enforces numeric(19,6) database type and MidpointRounding.ToEven in calculators", "End-of-Service Benefits Provision Calculation: End-of-service benefits accrued as a provision entered through ledger maker and checker; platform calculates no autonomous estimate without approved policy. StaffProvisionLedgerService records provision via maker-checker; autonomous calculation disabled"])])
exSrcHead = CardHeader("Supplied source mappings", "Citation, authority label and code alignment per supplied module")
